{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And Elohim blessed Yitzchak his son.</b> He did not wish to bless him during Avraham's lifetime, because the Holy One, blessed be He, had already said to Avraham, ״וֶהְיֵה בְּרָכָה״ (Genesis 12:2) — 'the blessings are in your hand,' so how could the Holy One, blessed be He, take from his hand what He had already given him? And Avraham did not wish to bless Yitzchak, for he was afraid lest Esav too be included in the blessing. And since Scripture does not specify with what He blessed him, and furthermore the word ״בְּנוֹ״ ('his son') is superfluous — for do we not yet know that Yitzchak was his son? — we may say that He blessed him that he would be 'his son' for every matter — he alone, and not the sons of the concubines, for they are as though they are not his sons; rather Yitzchak alone would be called 'his son,' and to him the right of inheritance."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:29:53.584460484Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}